    "chunk_text": "This reportedly was due to two reasons. One was that political parties were not willing to throw in their lot with the untested,unproven new kid on the block. The second was Vijay\u2019s insistence that he alone should be the chief minster. Unable to secure any ally, Vijay made a virtue of necessity by announcing last week that the party would go it alone at the elections.\n\nWhatever these electoral calculations may be, a recent , unexpected turn of events has caused a major upheaval. A personal matter  concerning Vijay is creating much controversy. Since this personal issue has political ramifications, it is necessary to delve into this \u201c domestic discord\u201d  matter briefly.\n\nAs stated earlier, Vijay\u2019s wife is Sangeetha Sornalingam a British national of Sri Lankan Tamil origin. In recent times there have been many rumours and \u201cgossip\u201dnews items about both being estranged. It was alleged that an extra-marital relationship between Vijay and another actress was the reason.\n\nThese rumours were proven true  when Sanggetha filed for divorce in February 2025. The following  excerpt from the \u201cIndian Express\u201dof 27th Feb 2026 stated as follows \u2013\n\n\u201cA divorce petition has been filed before the District Court at Chengalpattu seeking dissolution of marriage between Sangeetha Vijay and actor-politician Vijay (Joseph Vijay Chandrasekhar) under Sections 27(1)(a), (b), (d) read with Sections 36 and 37 of the Special Marriage Act, 1954.\u201d\n\n\u201cIn her petition, Sangeetha, states that the marriage was first registered in the United Kingdom on July 10, 1998. A ceremonial marriage was later solemnised on August 25, 1999, at Rajah Muthiah Mandram, Egmore, Chennai, according to Hindu customs and rites.\u201d\n\n\u201cThe petition states that the early years of the marriage were \u201ccordial and harmonious,\u201d with the petitioner devoting herself to the household and upbringing of the children.\u201d"
