    "chunk_size_bytes": 1075,
    "chunk_text": "Wycherley International School marks 40 years with coffee table book\n\nWycherley International School celebrated its 40th anniversary with the launch of a commemorative coffee table book, featuring four decades of educational excellence.Coordinating Principal Dayan Fernando described the project as a personal dream, intended to preserve the legacy of the school\u2019s founders, educators, and alumni for future generations.\n\nThe book captures the institution\u2019s journey from humble beginnings to a leading academy with about 4,500 students. Chairman Dr. Jagath Alwis and current Principal Dulka Mendis joined founders and staff at the launch, reaffirming the school\u2019s commitment to holistic education and strong student-teacher relationships.\n\nSamsung Sri Lanka launches Galaxy S26 Series with advanced AI\n\nAnalytics in focus as Prof. Steven Stern engages with Sri Lankan academia\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
