    "chunk_text": "Civilians living south of the Litani river and Beirut\u2019s southern suburbs have been ordered to vacate. Depopulation is underway, a prelude to repopulation and the extension of Israeli borders deep into Lebanon.\n\nIn the meantime, under the cover of Iran War, Israel has re-imposed starvation policy in Gaza and is expanding settlements in the West Bank.\n\nOn March 20, 2026, Israel attacked military bases in Southern Syria, ostensibly as retaliation for a Syrian attack on the Druze people in Suweida. According to a report by France 24, Israel drones are spraying herbicides on crops and even fruit trees in the buffer zone between Israel and Syria, destroying them.\n\nA Strategy for Israel was a 1982 essay written by right-wing Israel journalist Oded Yinon. Known as the Yinon Plan, it presented a series of measures to make Israel strong and safe. The first was the dismemberment of Egypt: using the Muslim-Christian split to set up a Coptic Christian state in Upper Egypt; \u201cBreaking Egypt down territorially into distinct geographical regions\u2026without a centralised state.\u201d\n\nThe second was the \u201cdissolution of Syria\u2026into ethnically or religiously unique areas,\u201d including a Druze state near the area of Golan Heights\n\nAs for Iraq, \u201cIraq\u2019s dissolution is even more important for us than that of Syria\u2026 An Iraqi-Iranian war will tear Iraq apart and cause its downfall at home\u2026\u201d The other recommendations included the \u201cdissolution\u201d of Saudi Arabia, invasion and occupation of Saini, the division of Lebanon, and the liquidation of Jordan.\n\nIn the four+ decades since the essay\u2019s publication, many of its proposals have become the reality, wholly or partially.\n\nThese regional transformations constitute necessary milestones on the road to Greater Israel, turning Israel into a regional empire by absorbing all or part of many a neighbouring land, including Egypt, Syria, Iraq, Turkey, Jordan, Lebanon and Saudi Arabia."
