    "chunk_size_bytes": 1849,
    "chunk_text": "Managers can use the experience of tranquility to recognise their constructive and destructive emotions. Constructive emotions such as happiness, cheerfulness, enthusiasm help us to\u00a0 progress. Destructive emotions such as anger, frustration, jealousy , on the other hand, retard our growth. Recognising the presence of both types of such emotions is useful to ensure self-regulation.\n\nThe\u00a0 more\u00a0 you experience tranquility, the more vibrancy you would have in your actions. This is vital\u00a0 for managers who have\u00a0 to maintain their\u00a0 energy in facing multiple challenges.\n\nTranquility invites you to strengthen your values. It reinforces deeply held convictions that enable you to form your character. \u201cA person that values its privileges above its principles soon loses both,\u201d so said Dwight D. Eisenhower.\n\nValues are associated with behavior. Oxford dictionary defines them as standards of behavior. Stephen Robins, a scholar in organisational behavior, describes them, as \u201cthe basic convictions that a specific mode of conduct or end-state of existence is personally or socially preferable to an opposite or converse mode of conduct or end-state of existence.\u201d In brief, it is a preferred way of thinking, feeling, and doing.\n\nExperiencing a deep inner silence will reinforce your values. This is crucial when the trend is to move away from values in search of quick financial \u201cvalue.\u201d\n\nWhen weird minds are at the helm of political positions, their decisions can affect multitude of innocent masses. This has been the harsh reality of war throughout the history. \"If a man speaks or acts with an evil thought, pain follows him. If a man speaks or acts with a pure thought, happiness follows him, like a shadow that never leaves him.\" This is what Buddha preached. In making it happen, one needs the inner stillness to begin with."
