    "md5": "f27a51d3258504b7ec152b74e03d2ac4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1817,
    "chunk_text": "Sohan \u2026 a total entertainer\n\nSohan Weerasinghe is, indeed, a legendary singer and entertainer, and what makes him extra special, to the ladies, in particular, is his captivating performances and versatility.\n\nAnd, guess what! The charismatic performer is off to Canada, this week \u2026 to woo the audience, in that part of the world, especially the ladies, they say.\n\nHis performances are always high-energy and engaging, and that\u2019s probably why he\u2019s so loved by fans of all ages! Yes, he has definitely earned his reputation as a crowd-pleaser!\n\nThe trip to Canada is for two engagements \u2013 Mega Stars Spring Blast Dinner Dance on 28th March, and Concert the following evening, 29th March.\n\nAll these engagements, he is now achieving, is as a solo artiste, and he has plenty coming his way.\n\nBefore his departure for Toronto, he did Richmond Night on 20th March, Royal College Group Sing-Along, and Battle of the Maroons, and on his return he will be in the spotlight at Ballad of the Warriors \u2013 a show for the Special Forces.\n\nBallad of the Warriors will be held on 11th April at the Grand Maitland Hotel, in Colombo.\n\nAll these engagements, as a solo performer, is definitely an indication that Sohan is a total entertainer. His energy is infectious, and he knows how to work a crowd.\n\nSohan Weerasinghe: A beloved figure in Sri Lankan entertainment / Sohan: Nowgoing solo\n\nSohan was the leader of the popular band Sohan and The X-Periments, blending Western melodies with Sinhala rhythms and creating a unique sound.\n\nEarly in his singing career, he was influenced by international artistes like Elvis, Engelbert, Tom Jones, and Cliff Richard.\n\nInitially, he pursued law but eventually chose music as his full-time career.\n\nSohan took over the band X-Periments in 1975, renaming it Sohan & The X-Periments."
