    "chunk_text": "Early in his singing career, he was influenced by international artistes like Elvis, Engelbert, Tom Jones, and Cliff Richard.\n\nInitially, he pursued law but eventually chose music as his full-time career.\n\nSohan took over the band X-Periments in 1975, renaming it Sohan & The X-Periments.\n\nSohan has entertained audiences, with his powerful vocals and engaging stage presence, in many parts off the world, including Australia, Canada, and the US, and has also collaborated with various artistes.\n\nIn fact, Sohan Weerasinghe is celebrated for promoting Sri Lankan music, globally, and inspiring aspiring musicians.\n\nHis contributions to the country\u2019s music scene are undeniable, and he remains a beloved figure in Sri Lankan entertainment.\n\nPirivenae Piyathuma \u2013 An authentic thought leader enters the heavenly passage\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
