    "md5": "e02f5065c317ae2b525a7d95c3480db7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1195,
    "chunk_text": "Tough time for local entertainment scene\n\nThe entertainment scene here is certain to feel the pinch due to the Middle East conflict, and petrol rationing.\n\nTourism, a big part of the country\u2019s economy, is taking a hit with fewer tourists arriving because of airspace closures and flight cancellations.\n\nThis is definitely affecting businesses, like hotels, restaurants, and entertainment venues.\n\nThe petrol rationing isn\u2019t helping either, but it is needed, at this point in time.\n\nWith limited fuel making it tough for people to travel and enjoy entertainment activities, the industry is certain to experience a decline in revenue and bookings.\n\nI\u2019m told that there are organisers who are contemplating making adjustments to their programmes, fearing that the crowd turn out will be poor.\n\nSome of the artistes have also mentioned that, the past couple of weeks, very few inquiries have come their way.\n\nOverall, I would say it\u2019s going to be a tough time for Sri Lanka\u2019s entertainment scene.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
