    "chunk_text": "Additionally, long-term success is also achieved through personal branding. Personal branding is long-lasting because, despite changing, improving, or declining business, personal branding will remain. Entrepreneurs with a large following and a personal brand that is successful will be able to recover and start new business ventures. Personal branding is not just limited to one business. However, it is essential to understand that personal branding is not just about pretending to be someone that one is not. Being genuine is part of what makes a personal brand successful. Consumers are able to differentiate between people who are trying to impress or copy others and those that are being genuine. Entrepreneurs should focus on being genuine and showing their true passions, values, and strengths.\n\nThere is much potential in personal branding in Sri Lanka. The youth are given an opportunity to showcase their skills and ideas to a larger audience through greater access to technology and interest in entrepreneurship. The youth can create powerful personal brands that focus on regional and international successes by combining creativity with communication skills. The message is clear at the end. The customer is not just buying a product in today\u2019s business world; they are buying a connection, trust, and authenticity as well. The business owners can create this by using personal branding.\n\nIn conclusion, the statement that \u201cbefore they buy your product, they buy you\u201d is a reflection of a fundamental reality that surrounds entrepreneurship in this modern era. The personal brand is essential in that it allows entrepreneurs to connect with their audience, make a long-lasting impact, and ultimately be successful. For one to be successful in business, personal branding is not just essential but a necessity.\n\n(The author is a 4th Year Undergraduate, Department of Entrepreneurship, Faculty of Management Studies and Commerce, University of Sri Jayewardenepura)"
