    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9bef360678c069bdb966d4876a38f1ce",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1424,
    "chunk_text": "E-entrepreneurship and E-business: Driving sustainability in digital economy\n\nIn a time characterised by swift technological progress and increasing concerns about the environment, e-entrepreneurship and e-business have surfaced as effective avenues to merge economic development with sustainability. But what do e-entrepreneurship and e- business truly signify, and why are they important in today\u2019s world? E-entrepreneurship involves entrepreneurial endeavors that are started, managed, and expanded mainly through digital channels, while e-business refers to utilising electronic networks to perform business tasks such as marketing, sales, customer support, and supply chain operations. Who participates in this change? Digital entrepreneurs, startups, established companies, consumers, and government entities all have crucial roles to play. Where does this transformation occur? Primarily in the online and virtual realm, transcending geographical limitations. When did it gain importance? It became significant with the emergence of the internet, mobile technology, and worldwide digitalisation. Most importantly, how does it relate to sustainability? By reducing physical resource consumption, lowering carbon footprints, and promoting innovative, eco-friendly business models, e-entrepreneurship and e-business offer solutions to pressing environmental challenges while fostering inclusive economic opportunities."
  },
