    "chunk_text": "In 2016, Muthukumarana co-founded Potenza, which has since evolved into an award-winning global technology consultancy with operations in Sri Lanka, Singapore, and Australia. The firm specialises in SAP consulting, data and analytics, and intelligent automation, delivering transformative, enterprise-grade solutions to a global client base.\n\nPrior to founding Potenza, Muthukumarana held several senior leadership roles across leading global and regional organisations.\n\nHis earlier career includes leadership roles such as Group Head of Information Technology at Hemas Holdings PLC, Enterprise Technology Specialist at Microsoft Corporation (Southeast Asia New Markets), and senior technology roles at John Keells Holdings PLC.\n\nMuthukumarana is an alumnus of the University of Oxford (Sa\u00efd Business School, UK), where he completed Executive Education in Strategic Innovation, ranking among the top performers in his cohort. He holds an MBA from the Postgraduate Institute of Management (PIM), University of Sri Jayewardenepura, along with postgraduate qualifications in IT, and is currently pursuing postgraduate studies in Financial Economics at the University of Colombo.\n\nHe is a professional member of leading global institutions including the British Computer Society (MBCS, UK), the Institution of Engineering and Technology (MIET, UK), and the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (MIEEE, USA). He is also a Certified Scrum Master (CSM), and an Enterprise Architect.\n\nIn recognition of his contributions to business and technology, Muthukumarana was named among Echelon Magazine\u2019s Top 100 Next-Generation Business Leaders of Sri Lanka (NE100) in 2019. He has played an active role in shaping Sri Lanka\u2019s digital economy through SLASSCOM, serving on national advisory committees for Intelligent Automation, and ICT Capacity Building, and as a General Council Member."
