    "chunk_text": "I have had the good fortune of listening to TMS singing on statge in Sri Lanka,India and Canada. Furthermore I had the opportunity of interacting with him personally many years ago when I was editing the Tamil weekly \u201cSenthamarai\u201din Toronto. I interviewed him  on the record for the  paper and then had dinner with him.He was in Canada for a stage performance .\n\nSoundararajan married Sumithra in 1946. They had three daughters and three sons, one of whom died at a young age. The other two sons are good singers too with voices similar to their father\u2019s.  TMS passed away on May 25, 2013, at the age of 90.\n\nTMS had been a resident of Mandaiveli in Mardras/Chennai since 1962.Hence the West Circular Road was changed to TM Soundararajan Road (Saalai)in his honour. Chief Minister Stalin personally unveiled the new name board in a symbolic gesture. A stamp too was issued in 2016   honouring him."
