    "md5": "84d9cdb6de60864dff372fb21cc747db",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1885,
    "chunk_text": "Cenmetrix achieves ISO 9001:2015 certification\n\nFrom left: Chittananda Kulatilake, Imran Ismail, Roshani Perera, Dewmi Gamage, Deshika Kushan and Vipula Chaminda\n\nCenmetrix recently achieved ISO 9001:2015 certification, the world\u2019s most widely recognised standard for Quality Management Systems (QMS). This significant milestone reflects the company\u2019s strong commitment to quality assurance, continuous improvement, and operational excellence across its technology solutions and services.\n\nFollowing the successful completion of all certification requirements and full conformity with ISO 9001:2015 standards, the official certificate was formally awarded to Cenmetrix in February 2026, marking an important step in the company\u2019s long-term quality and governance strategy.\n\nThe company\u2019s ISO journey began with a strategic decision to engage expert guidance to strengthen and transform its internal processes. Win Win Consultants Ltd. was appointed to introduce ISO best practices, define organisational quality objectives, and support process improvements, while TQCS International (Group) Ltd. was selected as the certification body to facilitate a structured and comprehensive certification process.\n\nAs part of the implementation process, organisation-wide awareness programmes were conducted covering ISO fundamentals, quality management principles, and workplace safety practices. These included fire safety training, first aid training, and occupational health and safety awareness sessions to reinforce a culture of quality, responsibility, and continuous improvement.\n\nUnder the leadership of the ISO implementation team, headed by Dewmi Gamage and Deshika Kushan, Cenmetrix established key QMS foundations, including clearly defined organisational structures, process maps, workflow documentation, standard operating procedures, and performance monitoring mechanisms."
  },
