    "chunk_text": "One unfortunate incident during this time was a misunderstanding surrounding Fr. Tissa Balasuriya\u2019s book\u00a0Mary and Human Liberation. Written within orthodox Catholic teaching but emphasizing the role of women in the modern Church, the book was controversially portrayed as heretical, leading to a Vatican order of excommunication. The Oblate order, which had its own highly qualified theologians in Sri Lanka, declared the work orthodox. After interventions by globally known theologians in dialogue with Fr. Balasuriya, the matter was resolved and the excommunication withdrawn. Fr. Aloy Pieris, in close consultation with Fr. Balasuriya during that time, witnessed how this controversy left a deep bitterness in a man known for a lifetime of commitment to the Church, including roles as defender of the Church during the school takeover issue and as director of Aquinas University College.\n\nThe characteristics of Fr. Aloy were his attachment to truth, boldness in stating it when necessary, and his constant observance of charity and love. He died at the age of 91. It is hoped that the work he left at Tulana\u2014preserving documentation and research\u2014will continue with the same dedication, as it represents a crucial contribution to developing local thinking and leadership for modern times."
